1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,460
Do you think that the writer passed his driving test? Why?
你认为作者通过驾驶考试了吗？为什么？

2
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:19,330
Do you think that the writer passed his driving test? Why?
你认为作者通过驾驶考试了吗？为什么？

3
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:27,730
I was being tested for a driving licence for the third time.
我第三次接受驾驶执照考试。

4
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:34,570
I had been asked to drive in heavy traffic and had done so successfully.
我被要求在交通拥挤的地方驾驶，我成功地做到了。

5
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:39,710
After having been instructed to drive out of town,
在接到把车开出城里的指令后，

6
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:42,590
I began to acquire confidence.
我开始有了信心。

7
00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:49,810
Sure that I had passed, I was almost beginning to enjoy my test.
确信自己已经通过，我几乎开始喜欢这次考试了。

8
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:57,070
The examiner must have been pleased with my performance, for he smiled and said,
考官对我的表现一定很满意，因为他微笑着说：

9
00:00:57,930 --> 00:01:01,040
'Just one more thing Mr.Eames.
“还有一件事，埃姆斯先生。

10
00:01:01,810 --> 00:01:07,720
Let us suppose that a child suddenly crosses the road in front of you.
假设一个孩子突然在你前面横穿马路。

11
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:15,670
As soon as I tap on the window, you must stop within five feet.'
我一敲车窗，你必须在五英尺之内把车停下。”

12
00:01:17,630 --> 00:01:21,700
I continued driving and after some time,
我继续开车，过了一会儿，

13
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:24,440
the examiner tapped loudly.
考官大声敲了敲窗。

14
00:01:25,740 --> 00:01:32,180
Though the sound could be heard clearly, it took me a long time to react.
虽然声音听得很清楚，我却过了好久才作出反应。

15
00:01:33,830 --> 00:01:39,580
I suddenly pressed the brake pedal hard and we were both thrown forward.
我突然使劲踩下刹车踏板，我们俩都被甩向前方。

16
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:43,890
The examiner looked at me sadly.
考官难过地看着我。

17
00:01:46,810 --> 00:01:54,380
'Mr. Eames,' he said, in a mournful voice,'you have just killed that child!'
“埃姆斯先生，”他用悲伤的声音说，“你刚刚把那个孩子撞死了！”
